identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.23914947"
    description: "Zenodo concept DOI for all software releases."
abstract: >-
  Testing an off-block Hessian correction alone can discard a combined step that lowers minibatch loss.
  The code and records compare the standalone, remainder-only and combined corrections at a fixed base step, then test whether shortening the remainder changes the choice.
  A reference based on diagonal-block norms separates changes in the curvature profile from changes in relative off-block mass.
